From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:25:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): list stored links under Links, and show each
 item's stored thread

A link the agent pins with sys_open_items_raise was stored but never
shown: the panel's rows leave links out, and the Links list read only
the chat. The Links list now pins every open stored link first, under
the title the agent gave it (a short form of the URL when it gave none,
including older rows titled by their URL), whether or not a loaded
message pins it; a closed stored link takes its pin and its page off the
list. Pins and pages the store does not hold follow as before.

A stored item is a thread, and its label in the chat only points at it.
An expanded row now shows the item's replies as the store keeps them
(the user's comments and the agent's replies, each once, in order), then
how it was closed, leaving out a resolution that only repeats the last
reply (StoredItemThread, which the chips' preview can reuse). The chat's
text no longer bears on a stored item: a label struck in the chat while
the store keeps it open is no longer flagged "closed in chat" or offered
for closing with the chat's sentence, and a closed item's chips describe
the close from the store. chatItemImport builds the import of one
chat-only label, for actions that record a single label.

Local only: extends the open-items-panel series, not proposed upstream
yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
